Imperial Edicts, Patents of Appointment, and Memorials (examinees to answer one):
Draft an imperial edict for Emperor Wu of Han calling for the recommendation of persons of flourishing talent and extraordinary caliber capable of serving as generals or ministers, or as envoys to distant lands (5th year of the Yuanfeng era [106 BCE]).
Draft a patent of appointment for Emperor Suzong of Tang appointing Guo Ziyi 郭子儀 as Secretariat Director (1st year of the Qianyuan era [758]).
Draft a memorial of congratulation on the auspicious appearance of a qilin.

Legal Judgments:
Recommending and presenting improper persons for office;
Missing the deadline for autumn grain tax;
Deviating from the direct route while traveling by post-relay;
Manufacturing not in accordance with regulations;
Delaying official documents beyond the prescribed schedule.

Third Session
Five Policy Questions
